<title>BELGIUM: AvH 1996 net profit jumps 66 pct.</title>
<headline>AvH 1996 net profit jumps 66 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year 1996</p>
<p>(In millions of Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit		     1,582  vs	951.4</p>
<p>    Net ordinary dividend (francs)	72  vs	 64</p>
<p>NOTE - Belgian holding company Ackermans &amp; van Haaren NV (AvH) said it booked a capital gain of 1.08 billion francs resulting from the merger of offshore oil services groups Forasol-Foramer NV and Pride Petroleum Services Inc.</p>
<p>But the total impact of the liquidiation and deconsolidation of Canadian subsidiary Consumers Distributing amounted 1.58 billion at the end of 1996.  </p>
<p>    Group own funds			7,828    vs    4,252.6</p>
<p>    Goodwill depreciation		  180    vs	 64</p>
<p>    Group net per share (francs)	 515.5  vs	309.3</p>
<p>NOTE - AvH said that taking into account the Pride transaction, group liquidity totalled 7.7 billion francs. Chief executive officer Luc Bertrand told a news conference that financial debt had been totally written off the books.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6815, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
